# TAIRiX CI/build-host crontab — sample.
#
# Works on any cron-based host (Linux cronie/Vixie, *BSD, macOS). On systemd
# Linux distros prefer the user units in tools/ci/systemd/ instead.
#
# Install with `crontab tools/ci/crontab.sample` after adjusting the repo path
# below. Every job is self-locating (it derives the repo root and puts the
# pinned toolchain on PATH via tools/ci/lib.sh), so the only thing to edit is
# REPO if your checkout is elsewhere (on Linux this is typically
# /home/<user>/... rather than the /Users/<user>/... shown here).
#
# A dedicated builder should track the branch tip: TAIRIX_CI_SYNC=1 makes each
# job `git fetch && git reset --hard origin/<branch>` before running. Drop it
# on a developer laptop where you do not want the working tree reset.
#
# Logs land outside the repo (default ~/ci-logs/tairix); override with
# TAIRIX_CI_LOGDIR. See tools/ci/README.md.

# On Linux change this to e.g. /home/<user>/RustroverProjects/tairix.
REPO=/Users/ianhawkins/RustroverProjects/tairix
SHELL=/bin/bash

# Full per-PR gate (AGENTS.md §7) every 30 minutes.
*/30 * * * *  TAIRIX_CI_SYNC=1 $REPO/tools/ci/ci-run.sh ci

# Nightly 24 h soaks — every §19.6 fuzz harness, §19.7 proptest model, and the
# §7 repeated-test matrix in parallel. One invocation; soak.sh fans them out.
0 2 * * *     TAIRIX_CI_SYNC=1 $REPO/tools/ci/soak.sh all

# Nightly headless Tier-1 builds (AGENTS.md §17.5) — the headless image must
# keep building for every Tier-1 target.
0  4 * * *    TAIRIX_CI_SYNC=1 $REPO/tools/ci/ci-run.sh build --headless --target x86_64-unknown-none
20 4 * * *    TAIRIX_CI_SYNC=1 $REPO/tools/ci/ci-run.sh build --headless --target aarch64-unknown-none
40 4 * * *    TAIRIX_CI_SYNC=1 $REPO/tools/ci/ci-run.sh build --headless --target riscv64gc-unknown-none-elf
0  5 * * *    TAIRIX_CI_SYNC=1 $REPO/tools/ci/ci-run.sh build --headless --target wasm32-unknown-unknown
